    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9136" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνο-ησία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
			<i>want of understanding,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀβέλτερος.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόησις,</span>
			<i>un-knowing,</i> i.e. mystical vision, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρεῖται ἀνοησία κρείττονι νοήσεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>mindlessness,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				44
			</span></i>.</div>
